From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jernej Skrabec <jernej.skrabec@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 18 Jul 2026 13:37:04 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] drm/sun4i: Share the DE33 DMA address space

All DE33 memory clients share one IOMMU master and must therefore allocate
and map buffers through the same device and domain.

Use the shared planes device as the DRM DMA device, allocate mixer RCQ
memory through it and defer writeback RCQ allocation until bind can
select that same DMA device.

Signed-off-by: Jernej Skrabec <jernej.skrabec@gmail.com>
[aiyengar: only the mixer and planes parts are carried: this tree has
 neither RCQ nor writeback, so the sun50i_wb.c hunks and the RCQ
 allocation are dropped. The planes device gets a 32-bit DMA mask
 instead of 40 bits, because the VI/UI fetch units here are programmed
 with the low 32 address bits only (no HADDR writes outside AFBC) and
 the IOMMU hands out 32-bit IOVAs anyway (LE's 40-bit mask goes with
 its 0239 IOMMU >4 GiB patch, not carried)]
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun50i_planes.c | 10 ++++++++++
 drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun8i_mixer.c   |  7 +++++++
 2 files changed, 17 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun50i_planes.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun50i_planes.c
index 2e0e7d36c..5a639669a 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun50i_planes.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun50i_planes.c
@@ -4,6 +4,7 @@
 #include <drm/drm_device.h>
 
 #include <linux/device.h>
+#include <linux/dma-mapping.h>
 #include <linux/io.h>
 #include <linux/mfd/syscon.h>
 #include <linux/module.h>
@@ -163,6 +164,15 @@ static int sun50i_planes_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	struct device *dev = &pdev->dev;
 	struct sun50i_planes *planes;
 	void __iomem *regs;
+	int ret;
+
+	/*
+	 * The VI and UI fetch units are programmed with the low 32 address
+	 * bits only. Behind the IOMMU all addresses are 32-bit IOVAs.
+	 */
+	ret = dma_set_mask_and_coherent(dev, DMA_BIT_MASK(32));
+	if (ret)
+		return dev_err_probe(dev, ret, "Cannot set DMA mask\n");
 
 	planes = devm_kzalloc(dev, sizeof(*planes), GFP_KERNEL);
 	if (!planes)
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun8i_mixer.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun8i_mixer.c
index 8783dabc5..6abada374 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun8i_mixer.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun8i_mixer.c
@@ -702,6 +702,13 @@ static int sun8i_mixer_bind(struct device *dev, struct device *master,
 		}
 
 		mixer->planes_dev = &pdev->dev;
+
+		/*
+		 * All DE33 memory clients share one IOMMU master. Use the
+		 * planes device for framebuffer allocations so they are
+		 * mapped in its domain.
+		 */
+		drm_dev_set_dma_dev(drm, mixer->planes_dev);
 	}
 
 	list_add_tail(&mixer->engine.list, &drv->engine_list);
